\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf1 While the two feeders below didn't perform as well as our picks for the best smart bird feeders, they offer some noteworthy benefits. Depending on your specific needs, you still might find them worthwhile.}{
\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2
\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf1 FeatherSnap Scout Smart Bird Feeder: This feeder has a solid, durable build, extra-large seed capacity, and an extendable perch that birds love to congregate on. However, its companion app could be more user-friendly. The bird identification process involves several extra steps, and unlike other apps that automatically display videos, you have to request each video. That said, I appreciated the app's "bird book" feature, which organizes your content and highlights facts about visiting species, such as their preferred seeds and region-specific information.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf1 Wasserstein Bird Feeder Camera Case: Unlike most smart bird feeders with built-in cameras, this model requires you to supply your own. It may be a practical option if you already have one of the seven compatible Wyze, Ring, or Blink cameras and don't need bird identification features. For testing, I paired it with the Ring Stick-Up Cam. While it's a solid motion-activated security camera, it was a poor choice for capturing birds. The footage was often blurry and out of focus, likely because the camera is designed for monitoring from more of a distance rather than close-up. Still, I appreciated the Ring app's customization options and its color night vision capabilities.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ql\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf1 What to look for in a smart bird feeder}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24
\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf1 To help make your decision easier and differentiate between the best smart bird feeders on the market, I interviewed two experts on the subject of feeding birds: Chad Witko, an ornithologist and specialist in avian biology at the National Audubon Society, and David N. Bonter, an avian ecologist and Arthur A. Allen director of citizen science at the Cornell Lab of Ornithology. Drawing on their insights, I compiled this list of key features to look for in a smart bird feeder.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf1 App features:}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf1  Smart bird feeder apps vary widely, so it's important to choose one that best matches your preferences. If AI identification is a priority, look for an app that not only identifies species but also provides educational insights or the ability to recognize and nickname specific birds. If you enjoy interacting with other birders, consider apps that allow you to share clips with a built-in social platform or invite friends and family to view your feed. Other features to consider include data storage limits, slow-motion settings, and safety alerts, such as notifications if a cat is nearby.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf1 Ease of cleaning:}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf1  A dirty feeder isn't just an eyesore; it can also harm visiting birds. "Feeders rapidly become soiled, and various diseases can be transmitted via feeders," Bonter says. Because regular cleaning is essential, he recommends choosing plastic feeders that are easy to take apart. In my experience, feeders with lots of nooks and crannies and ones that cannot be disassembled take much longer to clean. You'll need a long-handled brush to reach every spot. Wet and spoiled birdseed poses another health risk for birds, so Witko recommends feeders with drainage holes to discourage harmful mold growth.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf1 Convenient filling:}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf1  Since you'll be refilling your feeder often, convenience is key. Look for feeders with wide, easily accessible seed tray openings, ideally ones with roofs that lift or tilt out of the way so you can quickly fill and remount the feeder without spilling seed. Large-capacity feeders reduce the frequency of refills, while feeders that are easy to remove and reattach to the mounting hardware also streamline the process.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf1 Power:}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf1  All smart bird feeders run on rechargeable batteries, and how long they last depends on their capacity and the amount of activity at your feeder. To avoid the hassle of bringing the camera indoors to recharge, Witko recommends feeders with solar-powered batteries. Solar panels integrated into the feeder's roof or mounted separately keep the battery charged continuously. In especially cloudy regions, solar charging might not be as efficient. However, feeders with various power modes can help extend battery life, like BirdBuddy's power saver mode.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf1 Bird safety:}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf1  Whether traditional or smart, the best bird feedersshould prioritize the safety of visiting birds, a point both Bonter and Witko emphasize. Beyond preventing bacteria and mold growth, Bonter says you should also ensure your feeder can't trap or otherwise harm birds. Placement is also key to bird safety. "As a general rule, avoid placing feeders within 10 feet of any area that could conceal a predator, such as a cat, or act as a launch point for squirrels," Witko says. To reduce the risk of window collisions, position your feeder either more than 10 feet away from a building or closer than 3 feet.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
